            <ArticleTitle>Update on primary PCI for patients with STEMI.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-102</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1050-1738(16)30087-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.tcm.2016.06.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary PCI is the dominant reperfusion strategy for patients with ST-elevation myocardial infarction and continues to evolve. The purpose of this review is to summarize recent reports that focused on the relationship of door-to-balloon time with mortality, radial versus femoral artery access, aspiration thrombectomy, culprit versus multivessel primary PCI, drug-eluting stents, and anticoagulation and antiplatelet therapies.</AbstractText>
